course: dictionary
lesson: 12373
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Crude» is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The workers pumped crude oil from under the desert.» The clues are oil and pumping, so crude means oil that has not been cleaned or processed yet.
explain: «The children built a crude raft from logs and rope.» The clues are logs, rope and built. The raft is not neat or skilful, just simple and roughly made. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have probably found the right one.
explain: «He told a crude joke, and the teacher frowned.» The frown is the clue. The joke was rude and rough in a vulgar way. Crude can also mean rough and not exact: «The scientist gave a crude estimate of the crowd.» That is a quick, rough guess, not a careful count.
fact: Crude has several meanings, so always check the context to pick the right one.
fact: «Crude» can mean natural and unprocessed, as in «crude oil» taken from the ground before it is turned into petrol, diesel and plastics.
fact: «Crude» can mean simple and roughly made, as in «early tools were crude».
fact: «Crude» can mean rude or rough in a vulgar way, as in «a crude joke».
fact: «Crude» can also mean rough and not exact, as in «a crude estimate». Crude is also a short noun for crude oil.
exercise: «The workers pumped crude oil from under the desert.» What does crude mean here? | Rude and rough | Very expensive and shiny | Hot and dangerous | *Natural oil, not yet cleaned or processed
exercise: «The early people made crude tools from stone.» What does crude suggest? | Exact and carefully measured | Perfectly smooth and shiny | *Simple and roughly made
exercise: Mia says, «That was a crude joke!» What does she mean? | Simple and roughly made | *Rude and rough in a vulgar way | Natural and unprocessed | A quick rough guess
test: «The scientist gave a crude estimate of the crowd: about 500 people.» What does crude mean here? | *Rough and not exact | Rude | Simple and roughly made | Natural and unprocessed
test: «The pupils built a crude raft from logs.» Which meaning fits best? | Rude and vulgar | *Simple and roughly made, without much skill | Natural oil from the ground | Exact and carefully measured
exam: What does «a crude estimate» mean? | Exact and carefully counted | *A rough, quick guess that is not exact | Made from crude oil | A rude remark
